# Build contexts are the repository root, so keep out anything the images do
# not need. node_modules especially: the Dockerfiles run their own `npm ci`,
# and a host tree would carry the wrong platform's binaries into the image.
#
# Keep this file LF-only. Docker does not strip a trailing carriage return, so
# with CRLF every pattern here silently matches nothing and the entire tree —
# node_modules and gigabytes of .next cache included — is sent on every build.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.git
.next
**/.next
**/dist
**/.turbo
**/.cache
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Secrets never belong in an image layer.
.env
**/.env
**/.env.local

# Nothing a build reads.
docs
*.pdf
*.log
.vscode
.idea
